// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/group_view.t27 -- what the cabinet shows of group chat and what a click there means (owner, 2026-10-23;
// Refs gHashTag/t27#11560). Pure decisions only: no @extern, no socket, no clock. The groups, their logs and the
// fan-out are group_core.t27 and chat_host.t27; this file only lays them out.
//   * GROUPS N in the cabinet, under the friends and above the add part: a row a group (its name, how many people,
//     the unread badge); a click opens the group's chat. "+" at the right end of the label line opens NEW GROUP.
//   * NEW GROUP, a screen of the panel: the name (1..32 bytes, group_core gr_name_ok), the friends with a box each,
//     CREATE. CREATE stays muted and says why while no friend is ticked or the name is empty; a group is 2 to 8
//     people (1 to 7 friends and this device), as group_core.t27 allows.
//   * the group's CHAT, a screen of the panel drawn from the chat_view region (mode GV_CHAT): own lines right, the
//     others' left with the sender's nickname over the text, the time, and for own lines "sending", "sent",
//     "delivered to 2/3", "read by 1/3", "failed, will retry"; the field, Return sends, Esc goes back; an empty log
//     says "No messages yet. Say hello."
//   * unread per group: a badge on the row ("99+" past 99) and the sum in the head of the cabinet.
// Flat namespace (the window build splices imported modules): every name here starts with gv_ / GV_.
module T27osGroupView;

